<item>
            <title>[LU-20888] DNE MDT recovery hangs if MDS_CONNECT finds a thread pool fully blocked on osp_remote_sync</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20888</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When an MDT restarts while a peer MDT (MDT0000) is serving lookups for objects that live on the restarting MDT, MDT0000&apos;s regular mdt service threads all block in osp_remote_sync waiting on the restarting MDT. The restarting MDT&apos;s recovery then needs MDT0000 to accept its LWP MDS_CONNECT. That connect arrives with no export, so it is a normal-priority request, and the pool will not give it one of the threads reserved for high-priority work. It never gets serviced, the LWP never reaches FULL, FLD lookups can never be sent, and recovery waits forever.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="99700">LU-20888</key>
